question: is our 2x resampling worse than libjxl's? (re-run of the #102
  differential against the CORRECT reference version)
reference: cjxl v0.12.0 4279d48, built out-of-tree with -DJPEGXL_ENABLE_OPENEXR=OFF
  at ~/tmp/libjxl-v012-build. The earlier differential used the PACKAGED
  /usr/bin/cjxl, which is v0.11.1 — a different version with a different
  downsampler effort gate.
metric: the 2x resampling FLOOR = the best butteraugli either encoder's 2x
  regime reaches at any bitrate; min over --resampling=2 -e 7 at d in
  {0.3, 0.5, 1}. Scored at FULL resolution on a jxl-oxide linear decode,
  identical path for both encoders (jxlscore was cross-validated bit-identically
  against examples/distance_targeting_probe). butteraugli_main never used.
corpus: the same 8 centre-cropped (<=1024) images as the original differential.
result: mean ratio ours/cjxl = 0.994 (below 1.0 = ours better), range
  0.940-1.016. AT PARITY. The same measurement against v0.11.1 gave 1.095 and
  was read as a ~35% defect in our port; it was measuring the version gap.
  v0.11.x switches to the iterative downsampler between e5 and e7; v0.12
  restricts it to speed_tier <= kGlacier (effort 10-11) and our gate matches
  v0.12.
